        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: منصرف شدن",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "منصرف شدن (monsaref shodan) — \"to change one's mind, to give up an idea\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "او از سفر منصرف شد. u az safar monsaref shod. He decided not to go on the trip."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It takes az: az chizi monsaref shodan. Stem shav-."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "منصرف is usually traced to Arabic munṣarif \"turning away\"; with the Persian verb shodan \"to become\", you turn away from a plan."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
